#
# catalog -- what man.rapidcow.org publishes, and from where
#
# Two kinds of lines; fields are separated by blanks, `#' starts a
# comment.
#
#   release  DIST VERSION TAG [REPO]
#
#       A release is a tag in a Git repository.  ./snapshot copies
#       the pages of it into src/DIST/VERSION/ (with a RELEASE file
#       that says which commit that was), so that the build does not
#       need the repository.  REPO is the web view of the repository
#       (defaults to the one of the previous release line).
#
#   page     SECTION NAME DIST VERSION PATH
#
#       A manual page: NAME(SECTION), from PATH in the repository at
#       the tag of that release (so in src/DIST/VERSION/PATH here).
#
# The newest VERSION of each DIST (by the order of the release lines,
# so list them oldest first) is what /man/SECTION/NAME shows.  Every
# page here needs rules in Makefile.in and a line in MANIFEST, too.
#

#       DIST                              VERSION  TAG
release I18N-CodeSets                     0.00_00  HEAD  https://github.com/rapidcow/siteconf  # TODO
